@startuml

salt
{
  <b>ORE STUDIO - SYSTEM ADMINISTRATION: OPERATIONS</b>
  --
  <b>HOUSEKEEPING</b>  |  Stores (9) | Runs (3)
  --
  {
    Stores: 9 | Policies: 2 | <color:#b00020>Not bounded: 6</color> | Measured: 2.5 GB across 7 stores
  }
  --
  <b><color:#b00020>6 of the 9 stores have nothing that bounds them.</color></b>
  A store with no policy that applies is never deleted from. It grows until the
  database or the disk is full. The policies held today freed 0 B because nothing
  is older than its period yet; that does not bound the 6 stores below.
  [ Show the 6 stores nothing bounds ]   [ Open the runs log ]
  --
  <b>EVERY STORE</b>                                  [ Not bounded (6) ]   2 policies · 9 stores
  A store with no policy that applies is kept for ever.
  {#
    Store (shape) | Bounded? | Bounded by | Size | Growth
    Calendar dates (chunked) | <color:#b00020>Not bounded</color> | none -- no policy | 283 MB | +652 kB/wk
    Report run cashflows (chunked) | Bounded | drop chunks, 90 days | 186 MB of 512 MB | +16.9 MB/wk
    Report run metrics (chunked) | Bounded | drop chunks, 90 days | 4 MB | +372 kB/wk
    Market data delivery counts (ordinary) | <color:#b00020>Not bounded</color> | none -- no policy | 29 MB | +2.5 MB/wk
    Market data ticks (chunked) | <color:#b00020>Not bounded</color> | none -- no policy | 16 kB | flat
    Compute job inputs (prefix) | <color:#b00020>Not bounded</color> | none -- no policy | not measured | not measured
    Compute job outputs (prefix) | <color:#b00020>Not bounded</color> | none -- no policy | not measured | not measured
    Compute node scratch (host directory) | <color:#b00020>Not bounded</color> | none -- no policy | 1.9 GB of 2.0 GB | +145.7 MB/wk
    Engine package cache (package cache) | Bounded by keying | content digest | 209 MB | +19 MB/wk
  }
  --
  Each row also states the cost of having no bound: about 33 MB a year for the
  calendars and about 7.4 GB a year for the node scratch, at the rate of the
  last twelve weeks. A row opens that store's own page, where the plot,
  the policy and the activity are. The plot is not in the list.
}

@enduml
